    "bow": "FEAT-2326609804",
    "increment": 4,
    "comment": "engine.traffic (planned MOD) inc4 table: per-tile mode split keyed on (landUseDensityBand, localAccessBand). landUseDensityMapping buckets every SPECS id that carries residents or jobs (extracted from webconsole/src/sim/data.ts at HEAD 72474a7f) by (residents+jobs) magnitude into mode_share_by_density.json's own 8 band ids -- reusing that table's real-survey anchors rather than inventing a second density model (GR#3). The composite-key table then applies a small car->bus mass shift for local_access_low/_medium (a tile with local transit access diverts a slice of car trips to bus), renormalised to sum to 1.0 exactly per row. local_access_high (rail AND bus) rows are intentionally absent -- no bus/tram segment class is placeable yet (ASM-1533), so no tile can resolve to that band today; a tile that somehow does falls back to the city-level split (AC-3), which is the honest, non-fabricated answer for an unreached combination."
  },
