  "densityBandMagnitudeThresholdsNote": "BUG-989 fix (round 2): per-band MINIMUM (residents+jobs) magnitude, derived MECHANICALLY from landUseDensityMapping's own existing per-spec assignment (min magnitude of every spec currently mapped to that band, computed once by an uncommitted scratch script against webconsole/src/sim/data.ts's SPECS catalogue at the SAME HEAD landUseDensityMapping was generated from -- see meta.comment). Reconstructing every spec's tier-0 band via 'the highest threshold whose minMagnitude <= the spec's (residents+jobs) magnitude' reproduces landUseDensityMapping's existing per-spec assignment EXACTLY (verified: 0 mismatches across all 41 mapped specs) -- this is not a second, possibly-divergent density model, it is the SAME assignment re-expressed as a monotone step function of magnitude so the TS loader can evaluate it at ANY magnitude, not just the 41 magnitudes already in the catalogue. This is what makes the per-tile lookup TIER-AWARE (AC-1's 'use the TIER, not the raw capacityRaw field' requirement, BUG-989): a building's ACTUAL scaled capacity at its current capacityTier (capacityAtTier(spec, tier), data.ts) is looked up against these thresholds at runtime, instead of a fixed per-spec-id band that never moves regardless of upgrades."
